  faqs: [
    { q: 'How does Smartious compare to Dhirubhai Ambani International School (DAIS), TISB Bangalore, or BSD Delhi?',                                          a: 'Indian elite tier — DAIS Bandra Kurla Complex Mumbai (~INR 12-20+ lakh/year, #1 India, Reliance-established), TISB Whitefield-Sarjapur Bangalore (~INR 10-15+ lakh/year, 140-acre, top 5 India), The British School Delhi (BSD) Chanakyapuri (~INR 12-16 lakh/year, 66% A*/A IGCSE), American Embassy School Delhi (AES), plus JBCN Parel Top 40 IB globally, Ecole Mondiale (first India IB continuum), Pathways World School Gurgaon, Canadian International School Yelahanka (100% solar), Oakridge Nord Anglia network — provides physical campus premium international education with elite facilities and networks. Smartious provides live online Cambridge / IB / American / OSSD at USD 2,160-6,480/year (~INR 1.8-5.4 lakh/year) with identical qualifications, immediate enrolment, small class sizes (4-6 pupils), and cross-country cohort. Fee arbitrage substantial (4-16× cheaper); qualifications and international university pathway identical.' },
    { q: 'We\'re NRI family returning from Dubai/Doha/Riyadh/UK/US. How does Smartious support curriculum continuity?',                                        a: 'Very common Indian family situation. NRI returnee families with children in Cambridge IGCSE, A-Level, IB Diploma from Gulf (UAE DIS/DESS/GEMS/Nord Anglia, Saudi British International, Qatar British International, Kuwait American, Oman BSM), UK (Cambridge Home School Online, private schools), or US (American schools abroad, US public schools) continue seamlessly with Smartious — same Cambridge / IB curriculum without disruption. Avoids CBSE/ICSE conversion that would set student back 1-2 years. UCAS / Common App / OUAC university pathway maintained.' },
    { q: 'Is homeschool legally permitted in India?',                                                                                                          a: 'Yes. India\'s Right to Education Act 2009 (RTE Act) mandates compulsory education for children aged 6-14 through recognised schools but does NOT explicitly regulate or prohibit homeschooling — homeschool exists in a legal gray area, practically permitted. Smartious as accredited international curriculum provider delivers Cambridge / IB / American / OSSD qualifications recognised by Association of Indian Universities and international destinations.' },
    { q: 'Can we combine Smartious international curriculum with JEE / NEET / CAT preparation for Indian universities?',                                        a: 'Yes. Cambridge A-Level provides strong academic foundation for Indian competitive entrance preparation — A-Level Physics + Chemistry + Mathematics supports JEE Main/Advanced for IIT; A-Level Biology + Chemistry + Physics supports NEET for AIIMS medical entry; A-Level Economics + Business supports CAT for IIM. Some Indian families use Smartious as primary academic pathway with dedicated JEE / NEET / CAT coaching in parallel via specialist Indian coaching institutes (Aakash, Allen, FIITJEE, Resonance).' },
    { q: 'We\'re in tier-2 city (Ahmedabad / Chandigarh / Jaipur / Kochi / Coimbatore / Nagpur / Indore). Does Smartious serve us?',                            a: 'Yes. Smartious extends full Cambridge / IB / American / OSSD access to tier-2 cities without local Cambridge/IB physical schools. Live online delivery works via residential fibre infrastructure across all Indian tier-2 cities. Cambridge examinations sit at British Council venues or nearest metro authorised centres.' },
    { q: 'Where do Indian students sit Cambridge IGCSE and A-Level examinations?',                                                                             a: 'Cambridge Assessment International Education has authorised centres across India — British Council venues (Delhi, Mumbai, Bangalore, Chennai, Kolkata) plus dozens of authorised international schools accepting external private candidates in Mumbai (DAIS, Ecole Mondiale, JBCN, Oberoi), Delhi NCR (BSD Chanakyapuri), Bangalore (TISB, CIS, Indus, Oakridge), Hyderabad, Chennai, Pune. Smartious handles examination registration logistics.' },
    { q: 'How does live class scheduling work given IST and Nairobi teaching hours?',                                                                          a: 'India Standard Time (IST UTC+5:30) is 2.5 hours ahead of East Africa Time (EAT UTC+3). Smartious live classes 9 AM – 12 PM Nairobi teaching = 11:30 AM – 2:30 PM India local time — afternoon slot matching Indian school post-morning hours, practical for families combining local CBSE/ICSE/State board with international curriculum. Evening 5:30 PM – 8:30 PM IST slot also available. Recorded sessions 24/7.' },
    { q: 'We\'re Google India / Microsoft India / Amazon India tech corporate family. How does Smartious integrate with our rotation?',                        a: 'Indian tech corporate rotational assignment cycles (2-4 years typical). Smartious enrolment continues seamlessly through Bangalore/Hyderabad/Delhi NCR → Mountain View → Seattle → Dublin → London → Zurich postings without curriculum switching. Cross-country tech-family cohort provides social continuity.' },
    { q: 'What Indian cities does Smartious serve?',                                                                                                            a: 'Mumbai (Bandra Kurla Complex, Juhu, Parel, Powai, Andheri), Delhi NCR (Chanakyapuri, Vasant Vihar, Gurgaon Cyber City, Noida), Bangalore (Whitefield, Sarjapur, Yelahanka, Koramangala), Hyderabad (HITEC City, Kondapur, Gachibowli, Bachupally), Chennai (OMR, Kotturpuram, Perungudi, Anna Nagar), and Pune (Hinjewadi, Baner, Balewadi, Kalyani Nagar). Also broader India via live online delivery — Ahmedabad, Chandigarh, Jaipur, Kochi, Coimbatore, Nagpur, Indore, Lucknow, Bhopal, Vijayawada, Vishakhapatnam, Kolkata, and all other Indian tier-1/tier-2 cities.' },
    { q: 'What internet speed does Smartious require in India?',                                                                                                a: 'Sustained ~5-10 Mbps per student for live HD video conferencing. Jio Fiber, Airtel Xstream Fiber, ACT Fibernet (Bangalore + Hyderabad), Tata Play Fiber, BSNL Fiber, plus Reliance Jio 5G residential broadband across metros routinely deliver 100+ Mbps. Tier-2 cities with adequate ~10-50 Mbps broadband also supported.' },
  ],

